# Additional generated corpora. Same reasoning as data/: reproducible from the seed.
data-*/

# Pinned audit chain heads. Deliberately NOT committed: the whole point is that this file
# lives outside anything the application can rewrite, and a copy in the repository would be
# a copy the application's own deploy pipeline can rewrite. In production this is WORM
# storage; locally it is a file you keep, not a file you version.
audit-heads.txt

# Working notes and recording scripts. Kept locally, deliberately not submitted: they are
# scaffolding for building and demoing the project, not part of the system being reviewed.
# The deliverables are README.md, WRITEUP.md, docs/DECISIONS.md, and docs/CRASH_POINTS.md.
PLAN.md
PROGRESS.md
docs/DEMO.md
docs/DEMO_STEPS.md
docs/VIDEO_OUTLINE.md

# Per-file, per-method map. Duplicates the javadoc it describes, so it drifts; the code and
# README carry the same information without a second copy to keep honest.
docs/CODE_MAP.md
